        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Alma 51:8",
        "book": "Alma",
        "chapter": 51,
        "verse": 8
      },
      {
        "text": "But behold, this was a critical time for such contentions to be among the people of Nephi; for behold, Amalickiah had again stirred up the hearts of the people of the Lamanites against the people of the Nephites, and he was gathering together soldiers from all parts of his land, and arming them, and preparing for war with all diligence; for he had sworn to drink the blood of Moroni.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 124,
            "end": 134,
            "text": "Alma 63:14."
          },
          {
            "start": 350,
            "end": 355,
            "text": "Acts 23:12; Alma 49:27 (26–27)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 9,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "Alma 63:14.",
            "prettyString": "Alma 63:14",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "alma",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 63,
                    "end": 63,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 14,
                        "end": 14
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Alma 51:9",
        "book": "Alma",
        "chapter": 51,
        "verse": 9
      },
      {
        "text": "But behold, we shall see that his promise which he made was rash; nevertheless, he did prepare himself and his armies to come to battle against the Nephites.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 60,
            "end": 64,
            "text": "TG Rashness."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 10,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "TG Rashness.",
            "prettyString": "TG Rashness",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "studyHelp",
                "studyHelpType": "tg",
                "title": "Rashness",
                "entryId": "tg-rashness",
                "book": "",
                "chapters": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Alma 51:10",
        "book": "Alma",
        "chapter": 51,
        "verse": 10
      },
      {
        "text": "Now his armies were not so great as they had hitherto been, because of the many thousands who had been slain by the hand of the Nephites; but notwithstanding their great loss, Amalickiah had gathered together a wonderfully great army, insomuch that he feared not to come down to the land of Zarahemla.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 103,
            "end": 108,
            "text": "Alma 49:25 (22–25)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 11,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Alma 51:11",
        "book": "Alma",
        "chapter": 51,
        "verse": 11
      },
      {
        "text": "Yea, even Amalickiah did himself come down, at the head of the Lamanites. And it was in the twenty and fifth year of the reign of the judges; and it was at the same time that they had begun to settle the affairs of their contentions concerning the chief judge, Pahoran.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 12,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Alma 51:12",
        "book": "Alma",
        "chapter": 51,
        "verse": 12
      },
      {
        "text": "And it came to pass that when the men who were called king-men had heard that the Lamanites were coming down to battle against them, they were glad in their hearts; and they refused to take up arms, for they were so wroth with the chief judge, and also with the people of liberty, that they would not take up arms to defend their country.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 262,
            "end": 268,
            "text": "Alma 46:16 (10–16)."
          },
          {
            "start": 272,
            "end": 279,
            "text": "TG Liberty."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 13,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "TG Liberty.",
            "prettyString": "TG Liberty",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "studyHelp",
                "studyHelpType": "tg",
                "title": "Liberty",
                "entryId": "tg-liberty",
                "book": "",
                "chapters": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Alma 51:13",
        "book": "Alma",
        "chapter": 51,
        "verse": 13
      },
      {
        "text": "And it came to pass that when Moroni saw this, and also saw that the Lamanites were coming into the borders of the land, he was exceedingly wroth because of the stubbornness of those people whom he had labored with so much diligence to preserve; yea, he was exceedingly wroth; his soul was filled with anger against them.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 161,
            "end": 173,
            "text": "TG Stubbornness."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 14,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "TG Stubbornness.",
            "prettyString": "TG Stubbornness",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "studyHelp",
                "studyHelpType": "tg",
                "title": "Stubbornness",
                "entryId": "tg-stubbornness",
                "book": "",
                "chapters": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Alma 51:14",
        "book": "Alma",
        "chapter": 51,
        "verse": 14
      },
      {
        "text": "And it came to pass that he sent a petition, with the voice of the people, unto the governor of the land, desiring that he should read it, and give him (Moroni) power to compel those dissenters to defend their country or to put them to death.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 15,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Alma 51:15",
        "book": "Alma",
        "chapter": 51,
        "verse": 15
      },
      {
        "text": "For it was his first care to put an end to such contentions and dissensions among the people; for behold, this had been hitherto a cause of all their destruction. And it came to pass that it was granted according to the voice of the people.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 16,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Alma 51:16",
        "book": "Alma",
        "chapter": 51,
        "verse": 16
      },
      {
        "text": "And it came to pass that Moroni commanded that his army should go against those king-men, to pull down their pride and their nobility and level them with the earth, or they should take up arms and support the cause of liberty.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 17,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Alma 51:17",
        "book": "Alma",
        "chapter": 51,
        "verse": 17
      },
      {
        "text": "And it came to pass that the armies did march forth against them; and they did pull down their pride and their nobility, insomuch that as they did lift their weapons of war to fight against the men of Moroni they were hewn down and leveled to the earth.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 18,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Alma 51:18",
        "book": "Alma",
        "chapter": 51,
        "verse": 18
      },
      {
        "text": "And it came to pass that there were four thousand of those dissenters who were hewn down by the sword; and those of their leaders who were not slain in battle were taken and cast into prison, for there was no time for their trials at this period.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 59,
            "end": 69,
            "text": "Alma 60:16."
          },
          {
            "start": 174,
            "end": 178,
            "text": "Alma 62:9."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 19,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "Alma 60:16.",
            "prettyString": "Alma 60:16",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "alma",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 60,
                    "end": 60,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 16,
                        "end": 16
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "raw": "Alma 62:9.",
            "prettyString": "Alma 62:9",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "alma",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 62,
                    "end": 62,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 9,
